cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artefact, please cite it and the paper it accompanies."
title: "counting-laws: exact counting laws for anchor-based sparse attention and for supervision-bound tabular decision making"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hanxiaole666/counting-laws"
url: "https://github.com/hanxiaole666/counting-laws"
abstract: >-
  Artefact for the paper "Two counting laws for cost-sensitive decision systems".
  Contains an exact entry law for the causal window+sink+anchor attention mask, a
  linearity criterion in terms of the global-key budget, a block-granularity law
  for executed density, the GPU measurements that test them on a 6 GiB device, the
  language-model elicitation and low-rank-adaptation experiments, and the build
  chain that generates every number in the manuscript from stored result files.
  tools/countlaws.py needs no dependencies and reproduces the reference count.
keywords:
  - sparse attention
  - efficient inference
  - cost-sensitive learning
  - tabular decision making
  - small language models
  - reproducibility
authors:
